IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-nouns`
IMPORT `rra-logic`
IMPORT `rra-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `rra-part2-minimum-retirement-age`
IMPORT `rra-part4-remedies`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 -- TESTS for Part 4 (ss 8 to 8C).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the provision named beside it, before the assertion was run.
-- The worked employee is born on 1 January 1960 and attains the specified age of 63 on 1 January 2023.

`the worked employee` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS NOTHING
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

`the worked employee born on 29 February` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 29 2 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS NOTHING
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

`the worked employee who attained the specified age before 2012` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1940
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS NOTHING
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

`the worked employee whose contract stipulates a retirement age of 65` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS JUST 65
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

§ `Tests -- section 8, unlawful dismissal on the ground of age`

-- The class of section 8(1) is wider than the prohibition of section 4(2).  With a contract age of 65 the specified age is
-- attained on 1 January 2025 and the prescribed minimum retirement age on 1 January 2023.  A dismissal on 31 December 2024
-- is "below the specified age", so section 8(1) lets the employee ask the Minister for reinstatement; section 4(2) does not
-- prohibit it, the employee being past the prescribed minimum retirement age.
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the employee may make representations in writing to the Minister to be reinstated` `the worked employee whose contract stipulates a retirement age of 65` (Date 31 12 2024) TRUE (Date 31 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the employer may dismiss the employee on the ground of age before the prescribed minimum retirement age` `the worked employee whose contract stipulates a retirement age of 65` TRUE (Date 31 12 2024) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING


-- (1): "within one month of the dismissal", the same day of the next month
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the last day on which the employee can make representations to the Minister` (Date 15 12 2022) EQUALS Date 15 1 2023
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the last day on which the employee can make representations to the Minister` (Date 31 1 2022) EQUALS Date 28 2 2022
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the last day on which the employee can make representations to the Minister` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the employee may make representations in writing to the Minister to be reinstated` `the worked employee` (Date 15 12 2022) TRUE (Date 15 1 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the employee may make representations in writing to the Minister to be reinstated` `the worked employee` (Date 15 12 2022) TRUE (Date 16 1 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A late representation (16 January 2023) is outside the grant "within one month of the dismissal"; the subsection does not say it may not be made (NOTHING).
-- "below the specified age": dismissed on 31 December 2022 is below; dismissed on 1 January 2023 is not.
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the employee may make representations in writing to the Minister to be reinstated` `the worked employee` (Date 31 12 2022) TRUE (Date 31 1 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the employee may make representations in writing to the Minister to be reinstated` `the worked employee` (Date 1 1 2023) TRUE (Date 1 2 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the employee may make representations in writing to the Minister to be reinstated` `the worked employee` (Date 15 12 2022) FALSE (Date 15 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the employee may make representations in writing to the Minister to be reinstated` `the worked employee born on 29 February` (Date 15 12 2022) TRUE (Date 15 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) and (3)
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the Minister may direct the Commissioner in writing to inquire and report` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the Minister may direct the Commissioner in writing to inquire and report` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "before making a decision": once the decision is made the power has gone (ruled 2026-11-05 (a)); with no representations there is nothing to decide on.
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the Minister may direct the Commissioner in writing to inquire and report` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the Minister may direct the Commissioner in writing to inquire and report` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the Minister may direct the employer to reinstate and pay, or to pay compensation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the Minister may direct the employer to reinstate and pay, or to pay compensation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the Minister may direct the employer to reinstate and pay, or to pay compensation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the employer has complied with the direction of the Minister` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the employer has complied with the direction of the Minister` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the employer has complied with the direction of the Minister` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- TRACE-EXPECT: FULFILLED  (the employer complies)
#TRACE `s 8(3) the employer must comply with the direction of the Minister` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `comply with the direction of the Minister` AT 10
-- TRACE-EXPECT: RESIDUAL  (no compliance yet and the section states no number of days: the duty is still owed)
#TRACE `s 8(3) the employer must comply with the direction of the Minister` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)
-- (4): the five the Act names, "in particular"; the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the Minister must have regard to the consideration` `the loss sustained by the employee in consequence of the unlawful dismissal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the Minister must have regard to the consideration` `the employee's prospects in obtaining alternative employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the Minister must have regard to the consideration` `the steps taken by the employee to mitigate his or her loss` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the Minister must have regard to the consideration` `the period the employee has served with the employer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the Minister must have regard to the consideration` `the employee's age` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the Minister must have regard to the consideration` `the tripartite guidelines` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the Minister must have regard to the consideration` `the steps taken by the employer to re-employ the employee` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the Minister must have regard to the consideration` `any other consideration` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5), (6)
#ASSERT `s 8(5) the decision of the Minister on the representation is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(5) the decision of the Minister on the representation is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the employee may bring an action for damages in a court in respect of the unlawful dismissal` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(6) the employee may bring an action for damages in a court in respect of the unlawful dismissal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7): the offence, and a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both
#ASSERT `s 8(7) the employer is guilty of an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(7) the employer is guilty of an offence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(7) the penalty on conviction` EQUALS (Penalty OF 10_000, 12)
#ASSERT `s 8(7) the sentence is within the penalty` TRUE 10_000 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(7) the sentence is within the penalty` TRUE 10_001 12 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(7) the sentence is within the penalty` TRUE 10_000 13 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(7) the sentence is within the penalty` FALSE 10_000 12 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8): what remains unpaid is recoverable as if it were a fine, once the employer is convicted under (7)
#ASSERT `s 8(8) the amount recoverable by the court as if it were a fine` 5_000 2_000 TRUE EQUALS JUST 3_000
#ASSERT `s 8(8) the amount recoverable by the court as if it were a fine` 5_000 5_000 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(8) the amount recoverable by the court as if it were a fine` 5_000 2_000 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The yes-or-no twin: the "where" (an amount unpaid and a conviction) is not met, so no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 8(8) the court may recover the unpaid amount as if it were a fine` 5_000 2_000 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(8) the court may recover the unpaid amount as if it were a fine` 5_000 5_000 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(8) the court may recover the unpaid amount as if it were a fine` 5_000 2_000 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(8) the court may recover the unpaid amount as if it were a fine` 5_000 6_000 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (9) to (11): delegation
#ASSERT `s 8(9) the Minister may delegate the power` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(9) the Minister may delegate the power` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(9) the Minister may delegate the power` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(9) the Minister may delegate the power` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(9) the Minister may delegate the power` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(10) the delegation is revocable at will` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(10) the delegation is revocable at will` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(10) the delegation prevents the Minister from exercising the power` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(10) the delegation prevents the Minister from exercising the power` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(11) the power exercised by the delegate is deemed to have been exercised by the Minister` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "A power so delegated, when exercised by the delegate": a delegated power the delegate did not exercise is not deemed exercised by the Minister (ruled 2026-11-05 06:04 (c)); a power that was never delegated is outside the scope.
#ASSERT `s 8(11) the power exercised by the delegate is deemed to have been exercised by the Minister` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(11) the power exercised by the delegate is deemed to have been exercised by the Minister` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(11) the power exercised by the delegate is deemed to have been exercised by the Minister` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 8A, notice, mediation request and conciliation`

-- (4): a closed list of four matters
#ASSERT `s 8A(4) the dispute is a re-employment dispute` `denial of re-employment because the employee does not satisfy the eligibility criteria set out in section 7(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
